.nh
.TH "PB-DEVICE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-device - Manage devices


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb device [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage devices

.PP
List account devices, print a one-shot enrollment command, and manage one device's name, availability, capabilities, or revocation. All mutations are scoped to an exact enrollment; a device's online state does not by itself grant a service capability.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for device


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-device-add(1)\fP, \fBpb-device-availability(1)\fP, \fBpb-device-capabilities(1)\fP, \fBpb-device-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-device-rename(1)\fP, \fBpb-device-revoke(1)\fP
